{"name":"Stardust","hex":"#ddd3ae","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"stardust","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Small fragments of dustlike material found in space; specifically, a type of cosmic dust that formed from cooling gases ejected from presolar stars, which was then incorporated into the cloud from which the Solar System condensed.","Small fragments of dustlike material found in space; specifically, a type of cosmic dust that formed from cooling gases ejected from presolar stars, which was then incorporated into the cloud from which the Solar System condensed."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/stardust"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cosmic dust","blocks":[{"text":"Cosmic dust – also called extraterrestrial dust, space dust, or star dust – is dust that occurs in outer space or has fallen onto Earth. Most cosmic dust particles measure between a few molecules and 0.1 mm (100 μm), such as micrometeoroids and meteoroids. Cosmic dust can be further distinguished by its astronomical location: intergalactic dust, interstellar dust, interplanetary dust, and circumplanetary dust. Information on the nature of dust in locations beyond the Solar System is mostly obtained by methods of observational astronomy, such as photometry, polarimetry and infrared spectroscopy. Direct methods are also available for the collection and study of space dust within the Solar System. For example, the Stardust spacecraft collected cometary dust, and also detected some particles of probable interstellar origin, returning samples to Earth in 2006."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Porous_chondriteIDP.jpg/330px-Porous_chondriteIDP.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cosmic_dust"},{"title":"Music Sounds Better with You","blocks":[{"text":"\"Music Sounds Better with You\" is the only song by the French house trio Stardust, released on 20 July 1998. Stardust was composed of the Daft Punk member Thomas Bangalter, the DJ Alan Braxe, and the vocalist Benjamin Diamond."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/9/9f/Stardust%27s_Music_Sounds_Better_with_You%22.png/330px-Stardust%27s_Music_Sounds_Better_with_You%22.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Music_Sounds_Better_with_You"},{"title":"Stardust (2007 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Stardust is a 2007 romantic fantasy adventure film directed by Matthew Vaughn and co-written by Vaughn and Jane Goldman. Based on Neil Gaiman's 1999 novel, it features an ensemble cast led by Claire Danes, Charlie Cox, Sienna Miller, Ricky Gervais, Jason Flemyng, Rupert Everett, Peter O'Toole, Michelle Pfeiffer and Robert De Niro, with narration by Ian McKellen."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/6f/Stardust_promo_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stardust_(2007_film)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_dust_formation_around_a_supernova_explosion.jpg/500px-Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_dust_formation_around_a_supernova_explosion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_dust_formation_around_a_supernova_explosion.jpg/1280px-Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_dust_formation_around_a_supernova_explosion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_dust_formation_around_a_supernova_explosion.jpg/500px-Artist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_dust_formation_around_a_supernova_explosion.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's impression of dust formation around a supernova explosion.[18]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArtist%E2%80%99s_impression_of_dust_formation_around_a_supernova_explosion.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Three_Bands_of_Light.jpg/500px-Three_Bands_of_Light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Three_Bands_of_Light.jpg/1280px-Three_Bands_of_Light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Three_Bands_of_Light.jpg/500px-Three_Bands_of_Light.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zodiacal light caused by cosmic dust.[20]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThree_Bands_of_Light.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Andromeda_galaxy_Ssc2005-20a1.jpg/500px-Andromeda_galaxy_Ssc2005-20a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Andromeda_galaxy_Ssc2005-20a1.jpg/1280px-Andromeda_galaxy_Ssc2005-20a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Andromeda_galaxy_Ssc2005-20a1.jpg/500px-Andromeda_galaxy_Ssc2005-20a1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cosmic dust of the Andromeda Galaxy as revealed in infrared light by the Spitzer Space Telescope.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAndromeda_galaxy_Ssc2005-20a1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Horsehead-Hubble.jpg/500px-Horsehead-Hubble.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Horsehead-Hubble.jpg/1280px-Horsehead-Hubble.jpg